# Env
# .env files are deliberately COMMITTED — this is a private repo and the same
# secrets are needed on several machines. Consequences to keep in mind:
#   - Anyone with read access to the repo has the Neon credentials, the Groq key
#     and the JWT signing secret.
#   - Git history is permanent. Rotating a key later does not remove the old one
#     from earlier commits; making the repo public would expose every version.
# If this ever stops being a solo private project, rotate all three secrets and
# switch to encrypted-at-rest secrets (git-crypt, age, SOPS) or a secrets manager.
# .env
# .env.local
# .env.*.local

